WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.090
Pause only where you are physically safe.

2
00:00:03.790 --> 00:00:05.950
Keep your eyes open if that feels steadier.

3
00:00:07.650 --> 00:00:11.210
You do not need to describe, analyze, or revisit what happened.

4
00:00:12.910 --> 00:00:19.600
This practice begins after the difficult moment and stays with the room, the body’s support, and your present choices.

5
00:00:21.300 --> 00:00:23.550
Stop or seek help if that is what you need.

6
00:00:30.265 --> 00:00:31.885
Look toward the edges of the space.

7
00:00:33.585 --> 00:00:38.255
Find the floor, the ceiling, the nearest wall, and the direction of an exit.

8
00:00:39.955 --> 00:00:42.525
Let your head turn slowly if that is comfortable.

9
00:00:44.225 --> 00:00:47.255
Notice that this place has shape and boundaries.

10
00:00:59.341 --> 00:01:06.071
Choose one object that feels ordinary: a cup, a door handle, a piece of fabric, a tree, or a patch of light.

11
00:01:07.771 --> 00:01:09.491
Notice its color and outline.

12
00:01:11.191 --> 00:01:13.761
Let something neutral have your attention for a few breaths.

13
00:01:27.190 --> 00:01:28.590
Listen for the nearest sound.

14
00:01:30.290 --> 00:01:32.250
Then the farthest sound you can hear.

15
00:01:33.950 --> 00:01:35.900
There may also be quiet between sounds.

16
00:01:37.600 --> 00:01:39.600
You do not need to identify their source.

17
00:01:53.030 --> 00:01:55.100
Feel one clear point of support.

18
00:01:56.800 --> 00:02:01.030
Press the feet gently into the floor, or let the seat and back meet their surfaces.

19
00:02:02.730 --> 00:02:08.589
Notice the response of the surface: solid, soft, warm, cool, still.

20
00:02:25.376 --> 00:02:28.726
Check whether the body wants more or less contact.

21
00:02:30.426 --> 00:02:37.976
You might wrap your arms loosely, place a hand on a steady surface, move farther from a doorway, or create more space around you.

22
00:02:39.676 --> 00:02:41.536
Choose only what feels appropriate now.

23
00:02:58.323 --> 00:03:00.693
Notice the breath without asking it to calm you.

24
00:03:02.393 --> 00:03:05.503
It may be quick, held, uneven, or already settling.

25
00:03:07.203 --> 00:03:10.653
Follow one inhale and one exhale as they are.

26
00:03:12.353 --> 00:03:14.063
Then return to the support beneath you.

27
00:03:30.849 --> 00:03:38.639
If an image, sentence, or echo from the difficult moment appears, name it simply: a memory is here, or a thought is here.

28
00:03:40.339 --> 00:03:41.449
You do not have to enter it.

29
00:03:43.149 --> 00:03:47.049
Look again at the ordinary object and notice one new detail.

30
00:04:03.836 --> 00:04:06.896
Let the hands make a small deliberate movement.

31
00:04:08.596 --> 00:04:12.966
Open and close the fingers, turn the palms, or touch thumb to fingertip.

32
00:04:14.666 --> 00:04:18.746
Feel that the movement begins when you choose and ends when you choose.

33
00:04:32.175 --> 00:04:33.765
Now move the feet or toes.

34
00:04:35.465 --> 00:04:38.575
If you are standing, keep your balance and support.

35
00:04:40.275 --> 00:04:44.765
Let the body receive a quiet message through movement: this moment includes choice.

36
00:04:58.194 --> 00:04:59.634
Name three present facts.

37
00:05:01.334 --> 00:05:02.804
I am in this room.

38
00:05:04.504 --> 00:05:05.774
My feet are supported.

39
00:05:07.474 --> 00:05:08.744
I can see light.

40
00:05:10.444 --> 00:05:15.054
Use facts that are true for you and leave out anything that is not.

41
00:05:31.841 --> 00:05:37.941
Notice whether you need warmth, water, distance, company, quiet, or practical help.

42
00:05:39.641 --> 00:05:41.391
The answer may be unclear.

43
00:05:43.091 --> 00:05:46.211
You are only checking; you do not have to act before you are ready.

44
00:06:02.998 --> 00:06:07.128
If one next action is obvious and safe, name it in a few words.

45
00:06:08.828 --> 00:06:11.178
I will sit here longer.

46
00:06:12.878 --> 00:06:14.618
I will message someone.

47
00:06:16.318 --> 00:06:17.808
I will step outside.

48
00:06:19.508 --> 00:06:22.158
I will return to a familiar task.

49
00:06:23.858 --> 00:06:25.948
Keep the action close and concrete.

50
00:06:42.734 --> 00:06:44.594
Feel the whole body in the room.

51
00:06:46.294 --> 00:06:49.314
Include the difficult sensations without making them the center.

52
00:06:51.014 --> 00:06:55.724
Include clothing, temperature, support, sound, and the space beyond the skin.

53
00:07:12.511 --> 00:07:14.051
Take two ordinary breaths.

54
00:07:15.751 --> 00:07:18.301
On each exhale, notice the surface beneath you.

55
00:07:20.001 --> 00:07:22.481
On each inhale, let the eyes receive the room.

56
00:07:24.181 --> 00:07:27.691
There is no required feeling at the end of this practice.

57
00:07:41.120 --> 00:07:44.240
Look once more toward the exit and toward the place you will move next.

58
00:07:45.940 --> 00:07:48.260
Let the movement be slow enough to remain chosen.

59
00:07:50.660 --> 00:07:52.950
The difficult moment does not need to be resolved here.

60
00:07:54.650 --> 00:08:00.000
For now, you have returned attention to this place, this support, and the next available step.
